"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"An exact id match wins over every alias. App rows are never routable, so an installed app's keywords cannot shadow a menu route (htop ships Keywords=system)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-RGCV","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"The prelude's omarchy-pkg-present/missing shadows agree with pacman -Q everywhere. This covers provides resolution, version constraints deferred to pacman, and the no-argument case (present true of nothing, missing not)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"Scores tier exact label, whole-word app name, label prefix, label substring, name text, then description. Menus and links promote by 2, apps demote by 5 within a tier. Final order breaks ties by depth then declaration order."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-W17G","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"A value command shared by several guards (e.g. omarchy-default-browser across seven rows) runs once per batch, captured eagerly before any guard line."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Y58B","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"When no item declares a guard, the guard script is empty and no guard process runs."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z680","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["atomicity"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A"],"title":"mergeAppRows and swapProviderRows return fresh maps that drop orphan ids and the replaced batch. They list a duplicated incoming id once and never write into their input maps."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260928-8VJQ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["path_pair_agreement"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"A menu action may exactly match the bare-summon grammar: omarchy-shell shell summon <id>, plus an optional single-quoted payload. The payload carries no embedded quote and the id draws from [A-Za-z0-9._-]+. Such an action executes in-process via shell.summon(id, payload) instead of spawning bash. An absent payload defaults to an empty object literal, matching the bin/omarchy-shell argv default exactly. Any action outside that grammar falls back to the unchanged execDetached bash path. The fast path must preserve semantics: same plugin id, same payload bytes, same default."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling","external_call_timeout_bounded"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"All when/checked/disabled expressions evaluate in one batched bash run whose per-item results drive row visibility, checkmarks, and dimming."}],"total":19},"readiness":"not_assessed","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:6849bf0c5173df9a4c032c277bbbe7e2c44d26de26fa1c342a64e75ef30cb5fe","policyRevision":"87c3ca689c30eebd471559e1247520d2c5de8aff","role":"reviewer"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":19,"gatesAdvisory":27,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":178,"testsPassed":6},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbol` / line ranges (authored + derived) and function-local annotations; a whole-file trace is file-level (weak) and says nothing about which function a requirement needs.","Intent relations: requirement level =